# Financial domain

Source of truth: `docs/domain-model.md`, `docs/development.md` (how to add calcs), `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Calculation code MUST remain

- Deterministic
- Stateless
- Independently testable
- Free of I/O, HTTP calls, database access, and authentication state

## MUST NOT

- Guess, invent, or silently default required missing financial inputs in a way that hides incompleteness from the caller
- Couple calculation formulas to FastAPI, persistence, or farm database schemas
- Persist FinancialModel / Scenario state in this service (App Platform owns persistence — ADR-0003)

## Domain concepts vs code today

`FinancialInput`, `FinancialModel`, and `FinancialResult` are in-process types in `farm_functions/domain.py` for the annual P&L. HTTP still uses named functions and flat input dicts (`run_function`). `FinancialModel` is in-memory only (ADR-0003). Do not persist models here or make the domain types the HTTP surface unless the task explicitly changes the API contract.

## When changing inputs or formulas

- Read `docs/domain-model.md` for ownership and semantics
- Add/update `INPUT_FIELD_METADATA` (units, required, min/max, description); `FIELD_UNITS` is derived from it
- Document semantic meaning of new or materially changed inputs
- Add or update tests for the financial behavior
